## Flameshot + ${VERSION}

Lightweight, optimized screen annotation with smart window detection, default WebP capture, integrated video/audio recording, and free anonymous cloud sharing.

### Key Features

- **Integrated Video & Audio Recording:** Record any selected screen region or window directly into high-quality MP4 (`x264` + `AAC`) with perfect A/V synchronization. Automatic output to `~/Video/flameshot-plus/`.
- **Pre-Record Floating HUD:** Dedicated 530px floating toolbar. Choose your audio source before recording: System Audio (auto-detects monitor sink including Bluetooth), Microphone, Mixed (System + Mic), or Muted.
- **Window Snapping (X11):** Instant geometry detection. Double-click or press `W` / `Tab` to snap the selection box to any window under cursor.
- **Free Anonymous Cloud Upload (0x0.st / Catbox):** Dead Imgur API keys removed. Upload any screenshot with 1-click directly to **0x0.st** with automatic fast fallback to **Catbox.moe**. Direct links copied to clipboard with notifications.
- **Default WebP Format:** Modern, lightweight screenshot format out of the box.
- **Build Optimization:** Compiled with `-O3`, `-flto=auto` (Link-Time Optimization), and dead-code elimination (`-Wl,--gc-sections`). Standalone binary is ~**1.6 MB**, `.deb` package is ~**670 KB**.
- **Debian Policy Compliant:** Package provides, conflicts, and replaces stock `flameshot` for seamless zero-conflict upgrades.
- **Automated Quality Assurance:** Pre-release automated verification across 10 test suites: cppcheck static analysis, virtual display Xvfb GUI lifecycle, concurrency safety, malformed geometry protection, binary security, zero-error configuration validation, and Debian Policy compliance.

---

### Quick Installation (Debian 12 / Ubuntu)

```bash
wget https://github.com/Svarkovsky/flameshot-plus/releases/download/${VERSION}/flameshot-plus_12.1.0-1_amd64.deb
sudo apt install ./flameshot-plus_12.1.0-1_amd64.deb
```

Or run the standalone binary directly:
```bash
wget https://github.com/Svarkovsky/flameshot-plus/releases/download/${VERSION}/flameshot-plus
chmod +x ./flameshot-plus
./flameshot-plus gui
```

